</textarea></div><p><strong>What will be the output of this program?</strong></p><ol class="pointsa"><li>{0, 0, 'a1', 0, 9}</li><li>{0, 'a1', 0, 9}</li><li>{0, 9, 'a1'}</li><li>{0, 0, 9, 0, 'a1'}</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(43)"><span id="btntext43">Show Answer</span></button> <button class="workspace" onclick="showworkspace(43)"><span id="btntext43">Workspace</span></button><div id="workspace43"></div><div class="testanswer" id="answer43"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> (c) {0, 9, 'a1'}</p><p><strong>Explanation:</strong> The output of this program is {0, 9, 'a1'}</p></div><hr/><p class="pq">44) Which of the following statements would create a tuple in python?</p><ol class="pointsa"><li>mytuple = ("apple", "banana", "cherry")</li><li>mytuple[123] = ("apple", "banana", "cherry")</li><li>mytuple = ("2" * ("apple", "banana", "cherry"))</li><li>None of the these</li></ol><button class="showanswer" onclick="showhide(44)"><span id="btntext44">Show Answer</span></button> <button class="workspace" onclick="showworkspace(44)"><span id="btntext44">Workspace</span></button><div id="workspace44"></div><div class="testanswer" id="answer44"><p><strong>Answer:</strong> (a) mytuple = ("apple", "banana", "cherry")</p><p><strong>Explanation:</strong> Option (a) is the correct syntax for a tuple. So, option (a) is the correct answer.</p></div><hr/><p class="pq">45) Study the following program:</p><div class="codeblock"><textarea class="java" name="code">mytuple1=(5, 1, 7, 6, 2)
